    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3182\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize payment of transportation aid to the South\nHuntington union free school district\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill authorizes the State Education Department to reimburse the\nSouth Huntington School District for a certain 2005-2006\ntransportation contract.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 validates all of the acts taken by the South Huntington\nschool district in connection with certain transportation contracts of\nthe 2005-2006 school year. Section 2 directs the State Education\nDepartment to consider such contracts valid and proper obligations of\nthe South Huntington school district.  Section 3 indicates that this\nact shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe South Huntington Union Free School District filed certain\ntransportation contract extensions for the 2005-2006 school year with\nthe New York State Education Department. The department claimed the\ndistrict filed these contracts in an untimely manner. All other legal\nrequirements with the contracts and contract extensions were met by\nthe district. Without the requested legislation, the school district\nwill receive a retraction of a portion of their 2006-2007\ntransportation aid.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThe South Huntington Union Free School District would receive a\nreduction in necessary transportation aid from the New York State\nEducation Department.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
