    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3182A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize payment of transportation aid to the South\nHuntington union free school district\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill authorizes the State Education Department to reimburse the\nSouth Huntington Union Free School District for a certain 2005-2006\ntransportation contract.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 validates all actions taken by the South Huntington Union\nFree School District in connection with certain transportation\ncontracts of the 2005-2006 school year. This section lists all those\ncontacts and states that the South Huntington must comply with these\ncontracts. Section 2 directs the State Education Department to\nconsider such contracts valid and proper obligations of the South\nHuntington Union Free School District.  Section 3 indicates that this\nact shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe South Huntington Union Free School district filed certain\ntransportation contract extension for the 2005-2006 school year with\nthe New York State Education Department. The department claimed the\ndistrict filed these contracts in an untimely manner. All other legal\nrequirements with the contracts and contract extensions were met by\nthe district. Without the requested legislation, the school district\nwill receive a retraction of a portion of their 2006-2007\ntransportation aid.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThe South Huntington Union Free School District would receive a\nreduction in necessary transportation aid from the New York Stated\nEducation Department.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
